# Scheduled jobs for the VPS. Install with:
#
#   crontab -e        (as the user that owns /opt/interlaken)
#
# Prerequisite, or every line below fails silently into a directory that does
# not exist:
#   sudo mkdir -p /var/log/interlaken && sudo chown $USER /var/log/interlaken
#
# Real cron honours */5 exactly. GitHub Actions was scheduled every 5 minutes
# but in practice fired about hourly, so this is a genuine improvement in how
# quickly a missed cafeteria webhook gets picked up.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
COMPOSE=/opt/interlaken/deploy

# A stock Ubuntu VPS runs on UTC, so "6 AM" here would fire at midnight local
# time. Pin the zone rather than doing the arithmetic by hand twice a year.
CRON_TZ=America/Mexico_City

# ── Cafeteria sync, every 5 minutes ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Order matters: seed opening balances for newly linked students BEFORE polling
# purchases, or a first purchase can land on a student with no balance row.
# flock prevents a slow Loyverse call from stacking runs until memory runs out.
*/5 * * * * cd $COMPOSE && flock -n /tmp/interlaken-loyverse.lock bash -c 'docker compose exec -T app python manage.py sync_balances --no-profiles && docker compose exec -T app python manage.py sync_purchases' >> /var/log/interlaken/loyverse.log 2>&1

# ── Daily tasks, 06:15 local ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ';' not '&&' on purpose: these are independent, and one failure must not
# cancel the reminders that follow it.
15 6 * * * cd $COMPOSE && flock -n /tmp/interlaken-daily.lock bash -c 'docker compose exec -T app python manage.py expire_stale_payments; docker compose exec -T app python manage.py low_balance_alerts; docker compose exec -T app python manage.py send_booking_reminders; docker compose exec -T app python manage.py dispatch_notifications' >> /var/log/interlaken/daily.log 2>&1

# ── Spending digest, 18:00 local ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately separate from the 06:15 block: the digest summarises the day's
# cafeteria spending, and at 06:15 that window is always empty. It also only
# does anything when CAFETERIA_PURCHASE_DIGEST is on; with per-purchase alerts
# enabled (the default) it is a harmless no-op.
0 18 * * 1-5 cd $COMPOSE && flock -n /tmp/interlaken-digest.lock docker compose exec -T app python manage.py send_spending_digest >> /var/log/interlaken/daily.log 2>&1

# ── Alert if the cafeteria sync stops running ───────────────────────────────
# Without this a broken sync is invisible for days: the site looks fine and
# balances just quietly stop moving. If the log has not been touched in 30
# minutes, something is wrong. Replace `mail` with whatever you actually read.
*/30 * * * * find /var/log/interlaken/loyverse.log -mmin +30 2>/dev/null | grep -q . && echo "Interlaken: cafeteria sync has not run in 30+ minutes on $(hostname)" | mail -s "Interlaken cron stalled" mustaphaukizuru@gmail.com

# ── Log rotation so the files above cannot fill the disk ────────────────────
# Nightly database backup at 02:30 (see backup-db.sh). The database now runs on
# this box, so nothing off-site backs it up: if this stops, there is no copy.
30 2 * * * cd $COMPOSE && flock -n /tmp/interlaken-backup.lock ./backup-db.sh >> /var/log/interlaken/backup.log 2>&1

# Shout if last night's backup did not land. Silence from a backup job looks
# exactly like success, which is how the previous one failed for five nights.
45 7 * * * find /var/backups/interlaken -name 'db-*.sql.gz' -mtime -1 2>/dev/null | grep -q . || echo "Interlaken: NO database backup in the last 24h on $(hostname)" | mail -s "Interlaken backup missing" mustaphaukizuru@gmail.com

0 3 * * 0 find /var/log/interlaken -name '*.log' -size +50M -exec truncate -s 0 {} \;

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub Actions: disable "Loyverse cafeteria sync" and "scheduled-tasks" once
# the above is running, or both fire against the same database. The work is
# idempotent so nothing is double charged, but the Actions runs also execute
# `migrate`, which can collide with a container restart.
#
# KEEP "db-backup" ENABLED. It is the only thing backing up the database, it
# does not conflict with anything here, and nothing on this VPS replaces it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
